        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Are paint thinner and mineral spirits the same thing?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "They do the same job but are not identical. Both are petroleum distillates that thin oil-based paint and clean brushes. Mineral spirits are more refined, with less odor and fewer harsh compounds; products labeled paint thinner are typically a less refined cut. Odorless mineral spirits go further, removing most aromatics. For oil paint, they are interchangeable."
          }
