          </p>

          <p>
            We also left things out on purpose. Generic paint thinner sold in plastic jugs works, but it carries more odor than odorless mineral spirits and offers no real advantage beyond a small price difference. We did not pick acetone as a paint thinner because it is not one for house paint, though we explain below where it does belong. And we did not include any product that promises to thin latex and oil paint alike, because that claim runs against how both chemistries work.
          </p>

