        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Most thinner questions answer themselves once you read the paint can. If it cleans up with mineral spirits, buy a can of odorless mineral spirits such as Klean-Strip, and use Penetrol when you want a smoother oil finish. If it cleans up with soap and water, put the solvent back and reach for water or Floetrol. Turpentine, Gamsol and bulk spirits are for specific jobs.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Measure what you add, stay inside the paint maker's reduction limit, settle and reuse dirty solvent, and take leftovers to household hazardous waste. Never pour thinner down a drain, and never leave oily rags in a pile. Do that and a single quart of the right solvent will last a lot longer than you expect.
          </p>
